# Trim the CLI upload to what the web build + MCP function need.
# The Tauri shells (esp. src-tauri/target ~2.2G) and scratch dirs are
# irrelevant to `npm run build:web` and the api/mcp function.
# NOTE: Vercel does NOT read .gitignore when this file exists, so anything
# gitignored-but-heavy must be repeated here or it uploads over the wire.

# Installed dependencies (~1.3 GB) - Vercel runs its own install during the build,
# so shipping the local tree's node_modules is pure waste and was the bulk of the
# ~1.2 GB archive upload (which flaky networks drop mid-transfer). Root + every
# workspace/submodule copy.
node_modules
**/node_modules

shells/tauri-desktop
shells/tauri-mobile
scratch
plans

# Scoped Chromium for the CLI/MCP Tier-B raster path (`lolly install-browser`),
# ~540 MB. Never used by the deployed function - esbuild bundles the MCP fn and
# includeFiles is only {tools,catalog}/**. Was the bulk of the 450 MB upload.
.browsers

# Prebuilt web output - Vercel regenerates it via buildCommand (outputDirectory
# is shells/web/dist), so shipping the local ~170 MB copy is pure waste.
shells/web/dist

# onnxruntime-web WASM runtime (~93 MB) - an EXACT copy of *.wasm/*.mjs from the
# installed onnxruntime-web dep's dist/. `build:web` runs `build:ort`
# (scripts/copy-ort.ts) to regenerate it from the dependency Vercel installs
# anyway, so uploading the local copy every ship is pure waste. Byte-identical.
shells/web/public/ort

# The transformers.js-pinned onnxruntime-web build (~31 MB, 4 files under a
# version-stamped dir). Same story as `ort` above, one directory over: the second
# half of `build:ort` (scripts/copy-transformers-ort.ts) recreates
# public/ort-hf/<pinned-version>/ from the installed dep on Vercel - the prod build
# log shows it doing exactly that, "copied 4 pinned onnxruntime-web runtime files".
# The version lives in the PATH, so a version bump writes a new directory rather than
# mutating this one - which is what makes vercel.json's `immutable` header safe here.
shells/web/public/ort-hf

# Model STAGING dirs (~686 MB - the single biggest slice of the ~2 GB suse upload,
# which is what makes the finalize-POST drop on flaky links). scripts/fetch-{matte,
# upscale}-models.ts stage a candidate OUT of the served tree, in .candidates/, for
# evaluation before it is promoted into its /models/<category>/ path. Nothing serves
# or references them: they are NOT in the precache manifest (the dist listing scan
# skips dot-dirs) and only the dev fetch scripts - which never run on Vercel - touch
# them. They reach the live site today only because vite copies public/ wholesale, and
# no client ever requests those URLs. Excluding them takes suse from ~2.0 GB to ~1.3 GB.
**/models/*/.candidates

# The served ONNX models themselves (~1.2 GB) - hosted by the dedicated static
# model-host project (deploy/models-host/, the lolly-models Vercel project) and
# reached through the `/models/:path*` rewrite in vercel.json, so the app deploys
# stop re-uploading unchanged model bytes on every ship. COUPLED to two things:
# the rewrite must stay in vercel.json, and shells/web/models-manifest.json (the
# committed listing scripts/gen-models-manifest.ts regenerates) must track the
# model set - it is what keeps /models/** in precache.json when the build has no
# model files on disk. Local dev and the self-hosted nginx deploy still self-serve
# from this directory; only the Vercel upload excludes it.
shells/web/public/models

# Profile views - derived from the packs (community/, brands/**), which DO ship.
# postinstall (use-profile --auto) rebuilds them on Vercel as real copies, so
# vercel.json's includeFiles globs and the web build's dist copy see real files.
/tools
/catalog

# Local sticky profile choice - a developer's `loldev profile <name>` selection.
# NEVER ship it: `loldev ship` archives the local tree, and use-profile --auto
# ranks the sticky file ABOVE the default profile. If it leaked into a deploy
# whose project has no LOLLY_PROFILE env, it would ship the developer's local
# brand (e.g. lolly-start) instead of the project's intended one - which once
# shipped the blank brand to lolly.tools. Each project's brand is pinned by its
# own LOLLY_PROFILE env var (or the `suse` default); this file is local-only.
/.lolly-profile

# Local Claude Code state (tool-permission config, a scheduler lock, and - the
# expensive part - agent WORKTREES, which are whole extra checkouts complete with
# their own dist/). Gitignored but rides an archive tarball otherwise.
# UNANCHORED on purpose: as `/.claude` this matched only the repo root, so
# shells/web/.claude/worktrees/<name> (133 MB, including its own 96 MB dist/ that
# the anchored `shells/web/dist` rule above also missed) shipped on every deploy,
# twice per ship. A bare pattern matches at any depth, like .gitignore.
.claude

# macOS Finder metadata. Tracked by nothing (the root .gitignore has `**/.DS_Store`),
# which is precisely why it kept shipping unnoticed: `git status` never mentions it
# and this file suppresses .gitignore, so ~40 of them rode every upload. One of them
# mattered - shells/web/public/.DS_Store, which vite's wholesale public/ copy carried
# into dist/ byte-identical (14,340 bytes) and the CDN then SERVED.
**/.DS_Store

# Hand-collected sample logos used for local testing (37 files, 500 KB). They carry
# THIRD-PARTY MARKS - Microsoft, NVIDIA, Deutsche Telekom Magenta, Collabora,
# Linagora - which are nobody's here to redistribute, and they sat in
# shells/web/public/ until 2026-08-25, publicly fetchable at /_testlogos/*. They now
# live in tests/fixtures/_testlogos/ with no code consumer anywhere in the repo; the
# pattern is unanchored so they stay off every deploy wherever the fixtures are kept.
**/_testlogos

# The docs-site screenshot MIRROR. docs/build.ts (build:info, run by build:web)
# rmSync's this directory and re-copies it from docs/shots on every build
# (build.ts:2519-2529), so the two trees are byte-identical - 146 files,
# 80,718,033 bytes each - and we were shipping both. docs/shots itself is tracked
# and still ships; this copy is derived. ~45 MB off each gzipped tarball (62% of
# it is SVG, which compresses ~71%, so it is NOT the ~105 MB a raw du suggests).
# NOTE: deliberately NOT excluding the sibling info/og. Those cards look equally
# generated, but generateOgImages() rasterises via Playwright Chromium, which is
# absent on Vercel, and - unlike build-tool-og.ts / build-view-og.ts - it has no
# process.env.VERCEL guard and its output is not committed. It fails soft and
# build() then derives ogSlugs from what exists ON DISK, so excluding info/og
# would silently drop the og:image from every /info page.
shells/web/public/info/shots

# The rest of the generated docs site: build:info regenerates every page, the
# sitemap and llms.txt from docs/*.md + docs/i18n/. ~27 MB off each gzipped
# tarball across 1,037 files. The tracked non-generated assets in info/ (icons,
# mascots, founded-by.svg - 152 files) are NOT matched by these patterns and
# still ship, which is why this is per-extension rather than the whole directory.
shells/web/public/info/*.html
shells/web/public/info/*.md
shells/web/public/info/**/*.html
shells/web/public/info/**/*.md
shells/web/public/info/sitemap.xml
shells/web/public/info/llms.txt

# Translation memory for scripts/translate.ts (13 MB, ~6 MB gzipped). A developer
# tool: no Vercel-side step invokes translate.ts, and the file stays git-tracked,
# so CI and local `npm test` / locales.test.ts are unaffected.
scripts/i18n/cache.json
